- How would you test exactly-once guarantees across regions?
- What happens if EventBridge fails to deliver cross-region events?
- How would you handle DynamoDB hot partitions in high-throughput scenarios?
- Design a schema for job dependencies and fan-out patterns.
- How would you implement distributed tracing across these services?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical serverless design, idempotency, error handling, and IAM least privilege in a real-world image workflow.

## Key Concepts

- S3 event triggers and Lambda integration
- Idempotent design using a dedupe key stored in DynamoDB
- Least-privilege IAM roles for S3, Lambda, and DynamoDB
- Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) setup for failed events

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal idempotent Lambda outline
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
// image processing omitted
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const rec = event.Records[0];
  const key = recs.s3.object.key;
  const jobKey = key;
  const exists = await ddb.get({TableName:'processed', Key:{jobKey}}).promise();
  if (exists.Item) return {status:'skipped'};
  // resize and store output placeholder
  await ddb.put({TableName:'processed', Item:{jobKey, t: Date.now()}}).promise();
  return {status:'done'};
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency under concurrent uploads?
- How would you monitor DLQ failures and ensure timely retries?

## Why This Is Asked

This validates practical isolation in a shared data lake, ensuring least privilege and scalable onboarding. It also tests policy layering and auditing capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- IAM roles per tenant with strict resource boundaries
- Trust policies tied to the tenant app identity
- S3 prefix-scoped permissions with bucket or IAM policy conditions
- Onboarding automation for new tenants and centralized governance
- Cross-tenant test plans and auditing hooks

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake",
      "Condition": {"StringLike": {"s3:prefix": "tenant-<tid>/*"}}
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-<tid>/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "<tid>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["sts:AssumeRole"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::<account>:role/TenantRole-<tid>",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "<tid>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this model to support cross-region backups without cross-tenant data leakage?
- How would you automate onboarding for new tenants without touching code (CI/CD policy issuance, audit log integration)?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-account access, tenant isolation, and end-to-end data export controls in a realistic setup.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account roles and STS AssumeRole with session tags
- S3 prefixes and object-level permissions
- TLS enforcement and per-tenant KMS keys
- CloudTrail auditing of cross-account activity

## Code Example

```json
// Trust policy for the tenant-scoped ExportRole
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": { "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::DATA-LAKE-ACCOUNT:role/ExporterRole" },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": { "StringEquals": { "aws:RequestTag/tenant_id": "tenant-123" } }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
// Tenant bucket policy sample for restricted CopyObject
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:PutObject","s3:PutObjectAcl","s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-123","arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-123/*"],
      "Condition": { "StringEquals": { "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption": "aws:kms" } }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this to dozens/hundreds of tenants?
- What are failure modes if the tenant account lacks KMS keys or if the ExportRole permissions are too permissive?
